From 65397093a59b93128febc12bae69d71bf72cada6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:01:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: passthrough backend step 2, the guest GPU VA space
 mirrored on the host GPU

EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH=1: the guest's GPU VA range [1 << 36, 1 << 40) is one RM
sparse range (unmapped addresses read 0 and drop writes instead of faulting).
GPU memory manager maps hand the backend runs of host memory (Eglantine's
device memory backing, imported as OS descriptors in 64 MiB granules on first
use) that it maps at the guest's own VAs; unmaps and sparse reservations unmap.
The guest's PTE kinds (nx2:gpu 211, 212, 213, 216) are kept per range and
mapped, compressible kinds as their incompressible fallback; a kind change
remaps what is mapped there. Guest memory is mapped GPU-uncached.

EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_CHECK=<n>: every n-th entry the host copy engine reads
the entry's words at their guest VA and compares them with what Eglantine
parsed and with the guest memory the mirror maps there.

With the backend on, HostMemory clears guest granules with memset instead of
punching holes in the memfd: a punched page stays pinned for the host GPU and
the file gets a new one (measured: the GPU read stale bytes for 4% of the
checked entries). EDEN_PUNCH_HOLE still overrides.

MKW, one race: 26898 maps, 16142 live RM mappings, 18422 kind changes,
7.4 GiB pinned in 1.5 s over the session; 128556 entries checked, 0 differ
from the mirrored memory (6 rewritten by the guest after parsing); no Xid,
RM client freed at shutdown. The guest's methods are still not submitted.
